---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import AppIcon from "../../components/AppIcon.astro";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { url } from "../../data/apps";
import icon from "../../assets/tattoo-stencil-maker/icon.png";
const software = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
  name: "Tattoo Stencil Maker",
  url: new URL(url("apps/tattoo-stencil-maker/"), Astro.site).href,
  operatingSystem: "Android",
  applicationCategory: "DesignApplication",
  description:
    "Prepare black-and-white tattoo stencils from imported artwork, with detail presets, mirroring and PNG or print-sized PDF exports. Android prototype in development.",
  image: new URL(icon.src, Astro.site).href,
  author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Velvet & Pixel" },
};
---

<Layout
  title="Tattoo Stencil Maker — Artwork to Stencil for Android"
  description="Prepare tattoo stencil artwork with Detailed, Balanced and Simple presets, original-image comparison, mirroring and PNG/PDF output. In development for Android."
  socialImage={icon.src}
  socialImageAlt="Tattoo Stencil Maker neon rose icon, split between solid artwork and clean outlines inside a teal frame"
  structuredData={software}
>
  <section class="wrap page-head product-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Tattoo &amp; Creative Tools / Android</p>
    <span class="status">In Development</span>
    <div class="product-title">
      <AppIcon src={icon} app="tattoo-stencil-maker" variant="product" />
      <h1>Tattoo Stencil Maker</h1>
    </div>
    <p class="intro">Your artwork. Ready for the next step.</p>
    <p>
      Bring your artwork into a focused stencil workspace. Compare the original,
      choose how much detail to keep, and prepare a black-and-white design for
      your tattoo transfer workflow.
    </p>
    <p class="availability">
      An Android prototype is in development and being refined with real
      artwork. A Google Play link will appear here when the app is publicly
      available.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section
    class="wrap section stencil-introduction"
    aria-labelledby="artwork-title"
  >
    <div class="stencil-mark">
      <Image
        src={icon}
        alt="A hot-pink rose changes from filled artwork to outlined petals within a luminous teal frame: the Tattoo Stencil Maker icon."
        width={512}
        height={512}
        widths={[320, 512]}
        sizes="(max-width: 760px) 80vw, 360px"
        format="webp"
      />
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">From artwork to transfer</p>
      <h2 id="artwork-title">
        Find the lines.
        <br />
        <em>Keep the character.</em>
      </h2>
      <p>
        Some designs need a little more detail. Others need room to breathe.
        Compare Detailed, Balanced and Simple presets, check the result against
        your original, and choose the direction that fits your artwork.
      </p>
      <p class="fine">
        These are prototype capabilities. Stencil quality is still being tuned
        with artist feedback; real-device and physical-print acceptance remain
        in progress.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="features-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">A focused artist workflow</p>
    <h2 id="features-title">Prepare it. Save it. Revisit it.</h2>
    <ul class="feature-summary">
      <li>
        Import PNG, JPEG or still WebP artwork using Android’s document picker.
      </li>
      <li>
        Compare Detailed, Balanced and Simple stencil presets, with a zoomable
        original-image comparison.
      </li>
      <li>
        Mirror the design and set paper and artwork width in your preferred
        units.
      </li>
      <li>
        Prepare A4 or Letter output, then export a PNG or a PDF sized for print.
      </li>
      <li>
        Keep local Saved Designs with optional names, detail choices and print
        settings; reopen them to regenerate the stencil.
      </li>
      <li>
        Process artwork on your device. The current prototype has no app server,
        account, billing or analytics integration.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="development-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">On the studio workbench</p>
    <h2 id="development-title">Built around real artwork.</h2>
    <p>
      Current work focuses on retaining useful outlines and structural folds
      while reducing unwanted shading and stray marks. Presets use local image
      processing and still need review across a wider range of designs.
    </p>
    <p>
      Large imports may be reduced in resolution. Print size and mirrored
      transfers still need physical-printer verification; this preview is not a
      guarantee of transfer quality or compatibility with every printer.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap callout">
    <h2>A stencil workflow worth talking about?</h2>
    <div>
      <a
        class="text-link"
        href="mailto:velvetandpixel@gmail.com?subject=Tattoo%20Stencil%20Maker%20enquiry"
      >
        Email the studio →
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={url("apps/")}>
        Explore the collection →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
<style>
  .stencil-introduction {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(28px, 6vw, 90px);
  }
  .stencil-mark {
    background: #000;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 24px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .stencil-mark img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .stencil-introduction {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .stencil-mark {
      width: min(100%, 360px);
      margin-inline: auto;
    }
  }
</style>
